        "problem": "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20614x}{x}.$",
        "worked_solution": "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{ln}\u20614x=\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }x=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20614x}{x} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{[\\operatorname{ln}\u20614x]^{\u2032}}{{[x]}^{\u2032}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
